      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\u0022paragraphs\u0022:[[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Keysight reported record third-quarter results, with revenue of $1.85 billion, up 36.54 per cent on a year earlier.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022GAAP net income for the quarter was $397 million.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Income from operations rose from $234 million to $461 million.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Communications Solutions Group revenue rose from $940 million to $1,345 million.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Wireline revenue exceeded wireless revenue for the first time in the quarter.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Management guided fourth-quarter revenue to a range of $1.93 billion to $1.95 billion.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Non-GAAP earnings per share for the fourth quarter are expected between $3.34 and $3.40, based on a weighted diluted share count of approximately 172 million shares.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The mid-point of the revenue range represents year-over-year growth of approximately 37 per cent.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Management said it is raising its outlook for the fourth quarter and for the full fiscal year.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The chief executive said supply chain will remain the governor of near-term revenue.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The chief financial officer cautioned that one-time tariff impacts lifted fiscal 2026 profitability and will not repeat.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Management\u0027s base case is for orders to be slightly up from the third quarter.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Analysts\u0027 tone on the call was slightly negative to pressing, with repeated questions on whether demand is sustainable and whether supply constraints limit guidance.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Shares rose in pre-market trading after the results, which beat Wall Street expectations for both earnings and revenue.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:2},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022Several analyst price targets sit substantially above the level at which the stock was trading.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:2}]]}"
